<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="curr-peanut" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Curried Peanut Soup</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell><term>Soup:</term></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 tablespoon butter</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 cloves of crushed garlic</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>1 cup finely chopped onion</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 teaspoons freshly grated ginger root</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon salt</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 cup chopped raw peanuts</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> teaspoon each:  cinnamon, cloves, ground cardamom or coriander</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoon each:  dry mustard, turmeric</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon ground cumin</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 cups stock</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cups natural peanut butter</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 tablespoon honey</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> to <m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoon cayenne pepper</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>1 \frac{1}{2}</m> cup room temperature buttermilk</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><term>Topping:</term></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 fairly green bananas</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 tablespoons lemon juice</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 tablespoons butter</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> teaspoon each:  cinnamon, turmeric</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>Dash of salt</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          In a large saucepan saute the first 5 items together over medium heat.  Add the peanuts and spices and saute, stirring another 10 minutes over medium low heat.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add the stock, peanut butter, honey, and cayenne to the saute.  Mix and cover.  Simmer over sheepishly low heat for 1 hour.  Stir occasionally.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Whisk the buttermilk into the hot soup just a few minutes before serving.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Peel the bananas and slice them thinly on the diagonal. Place them in a shallow bowl to bathe in fresh lemon juice. Let it stand 10 minutes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Heat the butter in a heavy skillet.  Add the bananas plus all their lemon juice, and sprinkle with salt and spices.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Fry, gently turning and stirring, 5 to 8 minutes over medium-low heat.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Spoon the topping into each individual bowl of soup.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>